::EM U4 p32 Review 1 MultiChoice:: Read the text below and decide which answer best fits each gap. There is an example at the beginning. <b>The science of happiness</b> Some scientisis believe that asking people how happy they are is  ____ asking them about an event they've attended in the past — there’s a lot they  ____ no notice of during the experience,so how do they know? These scientists think that anyone studying happiness should pay more  ____ to people’s experiences at the time they occur, not afterwards. Other scientists say that we are actually  ____ up of our memories. They suggest that studying moment-to-moment experiences at the time  ____ too much emphasis on temporary pleasures, and that happiness goes  ____ than that. They identify three key  ____ for happiness :  pleasure, engagement (how involved we are with family, work, romance and hobbies) and meaning (how we use our personal strengths to achieve important  ____. It is interesting that,  ____ to what might be expected, pleasure seems to play the smallest part in what makes us happy. {
	~against
	~opposing
	=contrary
	~contrast
}

